Add `kanban-md` to the `skills` metadata for `src/owlbear/agents/researcher.md` and `src/owlbear/agents/curator.md` so both agents can load kanban guidance through `SkillRegistry`. This task is limited to skill metadata and the tests that assert that metadata or the resulting skill-integration contract. See `docs/research/cheat-sheet-tool.md` section 4.

### Acceptance Criteria

1. `tests/test_agent_definitions.py` is updated first so `EXPECTED_AGENTS["researcher"]["skills"]` and `EXPECTED_AGENTS["curator"]["skills"]` both equal `["kanban-md"]`, creating the expected RED state against the current agent definition files.
2. `src/owlbear/agents/researcher.md` declares `kanban-md` as its only skill, using the same `skills` block-list format as other agents that load skills, with no changes to description, role, tools, or `max_delegation_depth`.
3. `src/owlbear/agents/curator.md` declares `kanban-md` as its only skill, using the same `skills` block-list format as other agents that load skills, with no changes to description, role, tools, or `max_delegation_depth`.
4. In `tests/test_pipeline_e2e.py`, `TestSkillsIntegration` no longer asserts `registry.definitions["researcher"].skills == []`; instead it asserts `registry.definitions["researcher"].skills == ["kanban-md"]` and `registry.definitions["curator"].skills == ["kanban-md"]` in the skills-enabled bootstrap scenario.
5. After the definition updates, the researcher and curator `test_skills_match` cases in `tests/test_agent_definitions.py` and the `TestSkillsIntegration` cases in `tests/test_pipeline_e2e.py` pass.
6. No `tools` entries are added or removed for researcher or curator in this task; enabling direct kanban or terminal execution is out of scope.

